yle races, swimmers may use any stroke they like.","t":"Rules","e":"\ud83c\udd93","f":"Almost everyone chooses front crawl, because it is the fastest way to swim.","a":true},{"k":"choice","i":"Which diving event, added to the Olympics at Sydney 2000, has two divers performing at the same time?","t":"Diving","e":"\ud83d\udc6f","f":"Pairs are judged on their own execution and on how closely their movements match.","o":["Team diving","Relay diving","Tandem diving","Synchronised diving"],"s":{"index":3}}]},{"slug":"how-many-players","title":"How Many Players?","tagline":"Water polo, netball, Aussie rules: count the players on each side.","emoji":"\ud83d\udd22","gradient":["#d97706","#b91c1c"],"categories":["sports","math"],"countries":null,"difficulty":"Medium","minutes":4,"questions":10,"prompt":"True or false?","yes_label":"True","no_label":"False","sort":350,"items":[{"k":"number","i":"How many players per team are in the water at once in water polo, including the goalkeeper?","t":"Pool","e":"\ud83e\udd3d","f":"Only the goalkeeper may touch the ball with both hands at the same time.","s":{"value":7,"tolerance":0,"min":1,"max":15,"unit":"players"}},{"k":"number","i":"How many players per team are on the ice at once in ice hockey during normal play, including the goaltender?","t":"Ice","e":"\ud83c\udfd2","f":"Teams swap skaters on the fly, and a typical shift lasts less than a minute.","s":{"value":6,"tolerance":0,"min":1,"max":12,"unit":"players"}},{"k":"number","i":"How many players does a baseball team have in the field while defending?","t":"Diamond","e":"\u26be","f":"The fielding positions include the pitcher, the catcher and three outfielders.","s":{"value":9,"tolerance":0,"min":1,"max":15,"unit":"players"}},{"k":"number","i":"How many players per team are on the field in a men's AFL (Australian rules football) match?","t":"Oval","e":"\ud83c\udfc9","f":"The women's AFLW competition uses 16 players a side instead, and both play with four posts at each end of the ground.","s":{"value":18,"tolerance":0,"min":5,"max":25,"unit":"players"}},{"k":"number","i":"How many players per team are on the pitch in Gaelic football?","t":"Gaelic games","e":"\u2618\ufe0f","f":"Players can run with the ball but must bounce it or kick it back to their own hands every four steps.","s":{"value":15,"tolerance":0,"min":5,"max":30,"unit":"players"}},{"k":"number","i":"How many players per team are on court at once in netball?","t":"Court","e":"\ud83e\udd45","f":"Each player wears a bib with letters such as GS for Goal Shooter or C for Centre.","s":{"value":7,"tolerance":0,"min":2,"max":14,"unit":"players"}},{"k":"number","i":"How many players per team are on the field in rugby league?","t":"Rugby","e":"\ud83c\udfc9","f":"Rugby league split from rugby union in northern England in 1895.","s":{"value":13,"tolerance":0,"min":5,"max":20,"unit":"players"}},{"k":"choice","i":"How many players are on each team in a game of polo?","t":"Horseback","e":"\ud83d\udc0e","f":"A polo match is split into periods called chukkas, and players often switch horses between them.","o":["4","5","6","7"],"s":{"index":0}},{"k":"choice","i":"How many players per team are on court in Olympic handball, including the goalkeeper?","t":"Court","e":"\ud83e\udd3e","f":"Only the goalkeeper is allowed inside the 6-metre goal area.","o":["4","5","6","7"],"s":{"index":3}},{"k":"choice","i":"In a rowing 'eight', how many people are in the boat in total, counting the cox?","t":"Rowing","e":"\ud83d\udea3","f":"The cox steers and calls the rhythm but does not row.","o":["7","8","9","10"],"s":{"index":2}},{"k":"order","i":"Order these team sports from fewest to most players per side.","t":"Team sizes","e":"\ud83d\udcca","f":"Curling teams have four players, and each one delivers two stones per end.","o":["Beach volleyball","Curling","Basketball","Canadian football"]},{"k":"order","i":"Order these sports by how many parts a standard game is split into (halves, periods, quarters or innings), from fewest to most.","t":"Match lengths","e":"\u23f1\ufe0f","f":"At the top level, netball's four quarters last 15 minutes each.","o":["Rugby league","Ice hockey","Netball","Baseball"]},{"k":"multi","i":"Select all the sports played with 11 players per side.","t":"Team sizes","e":"\ud83d\udd1f","f":"In cricket, all 11 fielders are on the field, but only two batters from the other side bat at once.","o":["Field hockey","Rugby league","Cricket","Netball","American football"],"s":{"indices":[0,2,4]}},{"k":"truefalse","i":"A men's field lacrosse team has 10 players on the field at once.","t":"Team sizes","e":"\ud83e\udd4d","f":"Indoor box lacrosse uses six players a side, including the goalie.","a":true}]},{"slug":"canada-beyond-the-rink","title":"Canada Beyond the Rink","tagline":"From the Summit Series to the Raptors: how well do you know Canadian sport?","emoji":"\ud83c\udf41","gradient":["#dc2626","#7f1d1d"],"categories":["sports"],"countries":["CA"],"difficulty":"Medium","minutes":4,"questions":10,"prompt":"True or false?","yes_label":"True","no_label":"False","sort":351,"items":[{"k":"multi","i":"Select all the sports named as national sports of Canada in the 1994 National Sports of Canada Act.","t":"National sports","e":"\ud83c\udde8\ud83c\udde6","f":"Ice hockey is the national winter sport and lacrosse the national summer sport.","o":["Ice hockey","Curling","Lacrosse","Canadian football","Baseball"],"s":{"indices":[0,2]}},{"k":"text","i":"Who scored Canada's series-winning goal in the final game of the 1972 Summit Series in Moscow?","t":"Summit Series","e":"\ud83c\udfd2","f":"His goal came with just 34 seconds left, after Canada had trailed earlier in the series.","s":{"accepted":["Henderson","Paul Henderson"]}},{"k":"number","i":"How many games were played in the 1972 Summit Series between Canada and the Soviet Union?","t":"Summit Series","e":"\ud83d\udd22","f":"Four games were played in Canada and four in Moscow, with Canada edging the series 4\u20133\u20131.","s":{"value":8,"tolerance":0,"min":1,"max":12,"unit":"games"}},{"k":"choice","i":"Sidney Crosby's 'golden goal' at Vancouver 2010 won the Olympic final against which team?","t":"Vancouver 2010","e":"\ud83e\udd45","f":"Crosby scored in overtime to seal a 3\u20132 win on the final day of the Games.","o":["Sweden","United States","Russia","Finland"],"s":{"index":1}},{"k":"number","i":"How many gold medals did Canada win at the Vancouver 2010 Winter Olympics?","t":"Vancouver 2010","e":"\ud83e\udd47","f":"It was a record haul for a single Winter Games at the time, after Canada had won no gold at its two earlier home Olympics.","s":{"value":14,"tolerance":0,"min":0,"max":20,"unit":"golds"}},{"k":"choice","i":"Which trophy is awarded to the champions of the Canadian Football League?","t":"Trophies","e":"\ud83c\udfc8","f":"First awarded in 1909, it is named after Earl Grey, then Governor General of Canada.","o":["Grey Cup","Vanier Cup","Memorial Cup","Allan Cup"],"s":{"index":0}},{"k":"multi","i":"Select all the rules that are true of Canadian football.","t":"Canadian football","e":"\ud83d\udccf","f":"The Canadian field is also bigger, measuring 110 yards between the goal lines with 20-yard end zones.","o":["Three downs to gain 10 yards","Four downs to gain 10 yards","12 players per side on the field","11 players per side on the field","A 100-yard field between the goal lines"],"s":{"indices":[0,2]}},{"k":"choice","i":"Which Canadian driver won the Formula One World Championship in 1997?","t":"Motorsport","e":"\ud83c\udfce\ufe0f","f":"He had also won the 1995 Indianapolis 500, and his late father Gilles was a Ferrari favourite.","o":["Gilles Villeneuve","Jacques Villeneuve","Lance Stroll","Nicholas Latifi"],"s":{"index":1}},{"k":"truefalse","i":"The Toronto Blue Jays won back-to-back World Series titles in 1992 and 1993.","t":"Baseball","e":"\u26be","f":"Joe Carter sealed the 1993 title with a walk-off home run in Game 6, only the second Series-ending homer ever.","a":true},{"k":"choice","i":"At Atlanta 1996, Donovan Bailey won Olympic gold and set a world record in which event?","t":"Atlanta 1996","e":"\u26a1","f":"His time of 9.84 seconds was a world record, and he added a second gold in the 4\u00d7100 m relay.","o":["200 m","400 m","100 m","110 m hurdles"],"s":{"index":2}},{"k":"choice","i":"In 1980, Terry Fox began his Marathon of Hope across Canada in which city?","t":"Marathon of Hope","e":"\ud83c\udfc3","f":"He ran about 5,373 km in 143 days on a prosthetic leg, and Terry Fox Runs now raise money for cancer research.","o":["Halifax","Vancouver","Victoria","St. John's"],"s":{"index":3}},{"k":"choice","i":"Which trophy, donated in 1892 by a Governor General of Canada, is now awarded to the NHL champions?","t":"Trophies","e":"\ud83c\udfc6","f":"Lord Stanley of Preston donated it as a challenge cup for Canada's top amateur hockey club.","o":["Stanley Cup","Hart Trophy","Conn Smythe Trophy","Calder Cup"],"s":{"index":0}},{"k":"truefalse","i":"Canada won the first Olympic women's ice hockey tournament, in 1998.","t":"Women's hockey","e":"\ud83c\udfd2","f":"The United States won in Nagano, but Canada then took the next four Olympic titles from 2002 to 2014.","a":false},{"k":"order","i":"Order these Canadian sporting moments from earliest to latest.","t":"Timeline","e":"\ud83d\udcc5","f":"The Summit Series was in 1972, Montreal hosted in 1976, Fox ran in 1980 and Crosby scored in 2010.","o":["Canada win the Summit Series","Montreal hosts the Summer Olympics","Terry Fox runs his Marathon of Hope","Sidney Crosby scores the 'golden goal'"]}]}]$d$; j jsonb; g jsonb; it jsonb; k text; begin if md5(d) <> 'd2ae080511fbd82c3da573aaf9167c27' then raise exception 'BAD_HASH'; end if; j := d::jsonb; for g in select * from jsonb_array_elements(j) loop insert into public.games (slug, title, tagline, emoji, gradient, categories, countries, status, difficulty, minutes, questions, prompt, yes_label, no_label, sort) values (g->>'slug', g->>'title', g->>